*.log
npm-debug.log*
bun-debug.log*

# Generated light-DOM stylesheet, built from the element sources.
helix/*/elements.css

# Generated sandbox page.
sandbox/ui/dist/
.vercel
.env*

# Generated vision film. Recapture with `bun tooling/scripts/capture-scale-film.mjs`.
site/ui/public/media/sovereignty.jpg
site/ui/public/media/sovereignty.webm

# Generated icon set, built from raw/.
helix/icons/src/generated.ts

# Dev server output, kept apart from the cached `.next` build.
.next-dev/

# Spec bundles for the sandbox, built from the spec files by `bun run specs`.
site/ui/public/specs

# The sandbox preview document, built from source by `bun run frame`.
site/ui/public/sandbox

# Worktrees an agent made for isolation. A second checkout of this repo, so
# tracking it would track everything twice and linting it collides with this
# tree's own root config.
.claude/worktrees/

# Measurement scratch: pages written to probe layout and paint, never shipped.
site/ui/public/.probe/

# The artifact a failed visual comparison leaves behind, marked with the pixels
# that moved. What belongs in the history is the baseline a reviewer approved,
# not the picture of a run that disagreed with it.
*.diff.png
*.parity.png

# Derived from the manifests and the example files by `bun run catalog`.
site/ui/content/catalog/catalog.generated.json
site/ui/public/helix/components/
site/ui/public/helix/docs/
site/ui/public/helix/*.md
site/ui/public/*.md
site/ui/public/insights/
# **The wasm is tracked, and it is the only binary here that is.** Every other
# generated artifact in this repository is committed and held to its generator by
# a check: `custom-elements.json`, `tokens.css`, `jsx.d.ts`. This one was ignored
# instead, which put a Rust toolchain on the critical path of anything that
# builds the site. CI could be given one. Vercel's build image cannot, and the
# site reads `public/helix/theme.wasm` from disk at build time, so a deploy that
# has to compile Rust first is a deploy that fails on a platform we do not
# control. Tracked, it is 419K that nothing has to rebuild.
#
# `check:wasm` is what keeps it honest, and it reads this artifact rather than
# building a fresh one first, so the file measured is the file that ships. It
# derives all seventeen themes through the tracked binary and holds them to
# `oracle.json`, which carries them as the TypeScript derives them. `cargo test`
# holds the host build to the same oracle. So the drift that tracking a binary
# invites, a derivation that moves while the committed artifact does not, fails
# here the moment the oracle is re-blessed.
